# Toniebox custom firmware @VERSION@

Revision @REVISION@. This package holds the custom firmware for both
generations of the first Toniebox and the setup page that belongs to it.

| File | For | Build |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `cc3200/ng-cfw.bin` | Toniebox with the CC3200 chip (SD bootloader slot image) | @CC3200_BUILD@ |
| `cc3200/ngbootloader.bin` | Toniebox with the CC3200 chip: the HackieboxNG SD bootloader with trial start and automatic return on updates | revision @BOOTLOADER_REVISION@ |
| `cc3200/flash/sys/mcuimg.bin` | its preloader for the flash of the box (`/sys/mcuimg.bin`) | revision @BOOTLOADER_REVISION@ |
| `cc3200/card/` | the SD card for a first installation: bootloader, its boot state file, this firmware in slot cfw1, the setup page, `ngCfg.json` set to start it | |
| `esp32/toniebox-cfw-esp32.bin` | Toniebox with the ESP32-S3 chip (app image) | @ESP32_BUILD@ |
| `setup.htm` | the setup page of the box (Wi-Fi, server, certificates), version @PAGE_VERSION@, needs at least @PAGE_NEEDS@ | |
| `SHA256SUMS` | checksums of the files above | |

Every file can be taken out of the package and used on its own.

## Install through teddyCloud (recommended)

teddyCloud with support for the custom firmware takes this package as it
is: Box Update > Library > drop the zip file (or let teddyCloud fetch the
GitHub release). Both images and the setup page go into the library; the
library shows when the setup page changed against the previous version.
Assign an image to a box or put it into the box's channel. The box
installs it at its next start; the setup page follows once it runs the
new firmware.

Do not pack the zip again: teddyCloud reads it only with its files stored
without compression, as published.

## Install by hand

**CC3200 box in the browser.** teddyCloud's web UI (web2, Box setup → CC3200)
installs a box from this package over the serial port: backup, certificates,
CA replacement and preloader, then it offers the content of the SD card as a
zip to unpack onto the card.

**CC3200 box (SD card).** For a first installation the preloader goes to the
flash (`cc3200/flash/sys/mcuimg.bin` to `/sys/mcuimg.bin`, after moving the
original `/sys/mcuimg.bin` to `/sys/pre-img.bin`), and `cc3200/card/` to the
card, plus the original `/sys/mcuimg.bin` of the box as
`/revvox/boot/ng-ofw1.bin`. The server goes into `/cfw/config.txt` on the
card (`host=`, `port=`).

To change a box that has HackieboxNG already, copy `cc3200/ngbootloader.bin`
over `/revvox/boot/ngbootloader.bin` on the card: this SD bootloader starts a
new image on trial and returns to the previous one when it does not come up.
Copy `cc3200/ng-cfw.bin` to `/revvox/boot/ng-cfw1.bin` and `setup.htm` to
`/cfw/setup.htm`. In `/revvox/boot/ngCfg.json` set, under `general`,
`"activeImg": "cfw1"` and `"stateFile": "/revvox/boot/ngstate.bin"`. The
server goes into `/cfw/config.txt` (`host=`, `port=`), or set it on the
setup page. The previous `activeImg` (usually `"ofw1"`) starts the original
firmware again.

**ESP32 box (serial port).** Keep a full flash dump of the box first. With
the box in download mode (J100 shorted at a cold power-on), write the
image into an app slot that does not hold the original firmware and
select that slot; see `esp32/README.md` of the firmware repository for
the commands. Never write the bootloader, the partition table, `nvs`,
`assets` or `phy_init`. The setup page is built into the image and is
replaced by teddyCloud later.

